Subject: [PATCH 127/144] perf(cuda): add GEMM vs cuBLAS relative-baseline
 harness (B3b)

Add scripts/smoke/cuda_gemm_baseline_smoke.py with three modes:
- measure: one independent G2 round (R=21 batched samples per side, fixed
  CPU affinity, clock assertion, in-run cuEvent rate calibration), G1
  correctness and per-case dispatch_seconds for the dispatch-dominated gate;
- g1: deterministic correctness only (exact-integer equivalence, pure-Python
  float64 oracle, full-shape exact-ones check), no timing;
- aggregate: three rounds -> candidate_ratio only (no lock/threshold files).

cuBLAS is bound through ctypes (Sgemm_v2 / GemmEx with
CUBLAS_COMPUTE_32F); the default case set covers 4096^3 and 2048x4096x4096
GEMMs plus two Qwen3.5-0.8B-shaped GEMMs expected to be dispatch-dominated.

No thresholds are frozen and no configs/perf_lock.yaml is touched.
