+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""CUDA GEMM relative baseline (PyPTO-X matmul vs cuBLAS) for the RTX 5080.
+
+This is the W8B B3b measurement driver.  It produces the G1/G2/G3 evidence
+required by ``docs/PERF_MEASUREMENT_PROTOCOL.zh-CN.md``:
+
+* G1 correctness -- independent references (exact integer arithmetic and a
+  pure-Python float64 oracle) plus a full-shape exact-ones check;
+* G2 stability  -- R=21 measured launches per case, one process per round,
+  three rounds, fixed CPU affinity, protocol variance gates;
+* G3 relative   -- only GEMM vs cuBLAS, ``ratio = pypto_x_median /
+  cublas_median`` over 3 rounds; the report only emits ``candidate_ratio``
+  (no thresholds are frozen here).
+
+Two modes:
+
+    measure   one independent round on GamePC WSL2; writes one JSON file;
+    g1        deterministic correctness only (no timing; usable in a
+              contended/interactive window);
+    aggregate combine three round JSONs into ``validation.json`` (local).
+
+The driver never writes any lock file.  Run it pinned to a fixed CPU set:
+
+    PYPTO_X_PORTABLE_ONLY=1 PYTHONPATH=python taskset -c 0-5 \
+        python3 scripts/smoke/cuda_gemm_baseline_smoke.py \
+        --mode measure --round 1 --json-out /tmp/round1.json
+
+cuBLAS is located at runtime (``/usr/local/cuda/lib64/libcublas.so.13``);
+no compiler or header is required.
+"""
+
